---
import { relativeLink } from '../utils/links';
---
<section class="section wrap" id="deployment">
  <div class="section-heading center-heading">
    <span class="eyebrow"><i></i> Your infrastructure, your choice</span>
    <h2>Native first.<br /><span>Container when it fits.</span></h2>
    <p>Proxyglass is a small Go service, not a platform you have to operate.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="deploy-grid">
    <article class="deploy-card deploy-primary">
      <div class="deploy-badge"><span></span> Recommended</div>
      <div class="deploy-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌘</div>
      <h3>Native binary + systemd</h3>
      <p>Install a static Linux binary, create a service account, and let systemd keep the dashboard running. Nginx remains responsible for TLS.</p>
      <ul><li>Linux amd64 and arm64 builds</li><li>Config in <code>/etc/proxyglass/</code></li><li>Optional DEB and RPM release packages</li></ul>
      <div class="deploy-note">One service. No Node.js runtime.</div>
    </article>
    <article class="deploy-card">
      <div class="deploy-icon container-icon" aria-hidden="true">▣</div>
      <h3>Container + Nomad</h3>
      <p>Prefer containers? Use the same config in a Docker image and schedule it as a small Nomad service.</p>
      <ul><li>Read-only HAProxy polling</li><li>Health endpoint for service checks</li><li>Persistent token storage is your choice</li></ul>
      <div class="deploy-note">Same app. Same config. Optional runtime.</div>
    </article>
  </div>
  <div class="deploy-card deploy-ansible">
    <div class="deploy-icon" aria-hidden="true">⚙</div>
    <h3>Ansible collection</h3>
    <p>Install and manage Proxyglass as code with the <code>chrisvanmeer.proxyglass</code> collection. It picks the right binary for your architecture, checks the temp mount for <code>noexec</code>, deploys a default config, manages systemd, and generates an admin token idempotently. Downloads honour <code>HTTP_PROXY</code>/<code>HTTPS_PROXY</code>.</p>
    <ul><li>Version independent of Proxyglass releases</li><li>Configurable temp dir and proxy envs</li><li>Molecule-tested with login verification</li></ul>
    <div class="deploy-note"><a href={relativeLink(Astro.url.pathname, '/docs/ansible')}>Read the Ansible docs →</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="airgap-note"><span class="airgap-icon" aria-hidden="true">◈</span><p><strong>Air-gap friendly by default.</strong> Dashboard JavaScript, styles and logos are bundled locally. For OIDC or external HAProxy targets, standard proxy environment variables are supported. Need a self-hosted Galaxy mirror? See <a href="https://getorbitron.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Orbitron</a>.</p></div>
</section>
